---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import client from '../config/client.ts';

const { company, contact, legal } = client;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  intro={`The terms on which ${company.legalName} provides this website and its services.`}
>
  <div class="legal-notice">
    <p>
      <strong>Placeholder text.</strong> This page is scaffolding so the site can
      ship with working compliance links. It has not been reviewed by a lawyer and
      is not legal advice. Replace it with terms drafted for {company.legalName}
      before going live, particularly the quotation, warranty and liability
      sections, which need to match what you actually offer.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>1. About these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms govern your use of this website and any enquiry you submit
    through it. By using the site you accept them. If you do not accept them,
    please do not use the site.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site is operated by {company.legalName} ({company.registrationNumber}).
  </p>

  <h2>2. Use of this website</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the site for any unlawful purpose</li>
    <li>Submit false, misleading or third-party contact details</li>
    <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to the site or its systems</li>
    <li>Copy or reuse site content without our written permission</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Enquiries and quotations</h2>
  <p>
    Submitting an enquiry does not create a contract. It is a request for us to
    contact you. Any indicative pricing shown on this site is illustrative only.
  </p>
  <p>
    A binding agreement is formed only when we issue a written quotation and you
    accept it. The quotation and its attached terms govern the work, where they
    conflict with this page, the quotation prevails.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Scope of works and variations</h2>
  <p>
    Work is limited to the scope described in the accepted quotation. Additional
    work discovered during a job, for example concealed water damage or
    substrate failure found once surfaces are opened up, will be quoted
    separately and requires your approval before we proceed.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Site access and preparation</h2>
  <p>
    You agree to provide safe and timely access to the property, and to obtain
    any approvals required from a management corporation, landlord or authority
    before work begins. Delays caused by access or approvals may affect the
    schedule and the price.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Warranty</h2>
  <p>
    Where a warranty is offered, its scope and duration are stated in your
    quotation. Warranties typically exclude damage arising from structural
    movement, third-party works, alterations by others, misuse, or failure to
    carry out reasonable maintenance.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Payment</h2>
  <p>
    Payment terms are stated in the quotation. Unless agreed otherwise, invoices
    are payable by the due date shown, and we may suspend work on overdue
    accounts.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Cancellation</h2>
  <p>
    Either party may cancel before work begins by giving written notice. Where we
    have already incurred costs, materials ordered, scaffolding erected,
    scheduled crew time, those costs may be charged.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Website content</h2>
  <p>
    We aim to keep the information on this site accurate and current, but we make
    no warranty that it is complete or error-free. Images of past work are
    illustrative; results vary with substrate, condition and specification.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect or
    consequential loss arising from your use of this site. Nothing in these terms
    excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded, including liability for
    death or personal injury caused by negligence.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    This site may link to third-party websites and services. We do not control
    them and are not responsible for their content or their privacy practices.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Personal data submitted through this site is handled in accordance with our{' '}
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of Singapore, and the courts of
    Singapore have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute arising from them.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms from time to time. The revision date at the top of
    this page shows when they were last changed. Last updated: {legal.lastUpdated}.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms can be sent to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a> or{' '}
    <a href={`tel:${contact.phoneHref}`}>{contact.phone}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
